* sg13g2-bandgap -- closed-loop PSRR (power-supply rejection) PEX
* (post-layout) PVT testbench (T1 tracker #4 item 7). Generated from
* sim/closed-loop-psrr-pex/testbench/tb_closed_loop_psrr_pex.spice.tmpl
* by sim/closed-loop-psrr-pex/run_pvt_sweep.sh -- do not edit a generated
* netlist-snapshots/*.spice file directly, edit this template and re-run
* the sweep. Full rationale is in sim/closed-loop-psrr-pex/README.md; this
* header is a pointer, not a restatement.
*
* Generated for: corner=fs temp=-40C vdd=2.97V
* DUT git sha (design/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, for XQ1/XQ2/XQ3, the
* only devices this bench still splices from a schematic):
*   core=d83f7c4 amp=397fe2d startup=66ac99d seeds=20260830-132425-d83f7c4.csv@94207b4
* Layout git sha (layout/bandgap_top/bandgap_top.pex.spice, extraction
* input for every MOS/resistor device and every wire parasitic):
*   8abe2aa
* PDK: ihp-sg13g2 /Users/rwalters/share/pdk (see sim/pdk.json for the pinned release)
* OSDI models: /Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi (built by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh)
*
* This file is the DEVICE/PARASITIC half of
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/testbench/tb_closed_loop_vref_pex.spice.tmpl
* (same extraction, same instance names, same wire-parasitic block, copied
* verbatim below -- see that file's header and
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/README.md for the full account of what the
* extraction does and does not model, not repeated here) driven by the
* MEASUREMENT half of
* sim/closed-loop-psrr/testbench/tb_closed_loop_psrr.spice.tmpl (AC
* injection on vdd, .nodeset-seeded .op, PSRR = -db(v(vref))). Only the
* three deltas below are new; everything else is one of those two files.
*
* DELTA 1 -- vsubs is tied to vss here, NOT through the 1 TOhm DC tie the
* transient/DC PEX benches use. Every extracted ground capacitance in the
* wire-parasitic block below returns to the node `vsubs` (the extractor's
* own substrate/far-plate convention). sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex and
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex tie that node to 0 through `Rvsubs_dctie
* vsubs 0 1e12` -- correct for their purpose (a DC/transient bench needs
* only a DC path, and 1 TOhm guarantees zero DC effect). That fixture is
* NOT adequate for a frequency-domain measurement: at AC, a 1 TOhm return
* leaves vsubs effectively floating, so every net's ground cap stops being
* a cap to ground and instead couples net-to-net in series with the other
* nets' ground caps -- which is not what the layout does. In this block the
* far plate IS the substrate, and the substrate is tied to vss (the same
* tie design/bandgap_core.sch's own `sub!` net carries, and the same node
* the extraction reports every device bulk terminal on). So this bench
* shorts vsubs to vss through a 0 V source. The measured size of that
* choice is quantified, not asserted, in
* sim/closed-loop-psrr-pex/README.md ("The vsubs tie matters here").
*
* DELTA 2 -- the transient vdd ramp is replaced by a DC supply carrying the
* 1 V / 0 deg AC stimulus, exactly as sim/closed-loop-psrr does; the loop is
* NOT broken (PSRR is a closed-loop property -- see that experiment's
* README "injection method"). The .nodeset seeds come from the same
* sim/closed-loop-startup record that experiment reads, and the per-point
* `op landed near its seed` check is applied identically here (the DC bias
* this AC analysis linearizes around must be the intended closed-loop
* equilibrium, not the degenerate all-off one).
*
* DELTA 3 -- the ammeter Vmkfb is kept (topology parity with every other
* closed-loop bench in this tree: it is a 0 V source, a DC and AC short,
* and moves nothing), but its current is not measured here -- this bench's
* measurement is the AC curve at vref.
.nodeset v(fb)=2.10833e+00 v(sns1)=7.84640e-01 v(sns2)=7.84614e-01 v(vref)=1.04729e+00

.lib "/Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib" hbt_typ
